      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Certainly. A standard three-step progressive discipline policy may initially involve a verbal warning to address minor issues; the second step could be documenting the behavior in writing, providing specific examples; if the issue persists, the third step might involve a formal written warning or coaching session with clear consequences. Following this, if interference continues, the final step might involve termination or further disciplinary action. It’s essential to document all steps meticulously.",
